---
import LegalShell from '../components/LegalShell.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalShell
  title="Terms of Use — Basebond Solutions"
  heading="Terms of Use"
  updated="21 November 2026"
  path="/terms"
  description="The terms that apply to your use of the Basebond Solutions website."
  intro="These terms govern your use of this website. They do not govern the professional engagement between you and Basebond Solutions — that is set out in a separate engagement letter."
>
  <h2>1. Use of this website</h2>
  <p>
    By using this website you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use
    the site. We may update these terms from time to time; the date above shows the latest
    revision.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information is general, not advice</h2>
  <p>
    The content on this site — including guides, checklists and articles — is general
    information about South African accounting, tax and compliance topics. It is not
    accounting, tax, legal or financial advice, and it is not a substitute for advice on
    your specific circumstances.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tax and company law change, and deadlines can be adjusted by SARS or CIPC. Always
    confirm current requirements on the official SARS or CIPC channels, or engage a
    practitioner, before acting.
  </p>

  <h2>3. No professional relationship</h2>
  <p>
    Sending an enquiry through this website does not create an accountant-client
    relationship. A professional relationship begins only when we have accepted an
    engagement in writing and completed the required client onboarding, including
    identity verification.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Pricing</h2>
  <p>
    Prices shown are indicative starting points for the packages described. They are not
    an offer capable of acceptance. Your final fee is set out in a written quotation after
    a review of your circumstances.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Accuracy and availability</h2>
  <p>
    We take care to keep the site accurate and available, but we do not warrant that it
    will be error-free or uninterrupted. We may change, suspend or withdraw any part of
    the site without notice.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The text, layout, design, graphics and code on this site are owned by or licensed to
    {site.legalName}. You may read, print and share pages for personal or internal
    business use. You may not republish substantial parts commercially without written
    permission.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    The site may link to third-party websites, including SARS, CIPC and the Information
    Regulator. We do not control those sites and are not responsible for their content or
    their handling of your information.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, {site.legalName} is not liable for any loss or
    damage arising from your use of, or reliance on, the general information on this site.
    Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited, including
    under the Consumer Protection Act 68 of 2008 where it applies.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our handling of personal information is described in the
    <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of South Africa, and the South
    African courts have jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms can be sent to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalShell>
